// Function: processInput
// Purpose: Accepts user input and processes it.
// Note the correct usage of "accept" (to receive input)
// and "except" (ignoring unwanted characters).
//
// Incorrect usage example:
//   // Accept the invalid characters except alphabets.
// Corrected documentation example:
function processInput(input) {
    // Accept (receive) user input.
    // Remove any characters except alphabets.
    let cleanedInput = input.replace(/[^a-zA-Z]/g, "");
    return cleanedInput;
}
Conclusion
Understanding and avoiding common vocabulary mistakes is essential for clear and effective communication. By adhering to best practices such as thorough proofreading, using reference tools, and continuous practice, you can significantly enhance the accuracy of your language use. Remember that vigilance in writing and attentiveness to context will help foster better writing habits over time.

